      "message": "test(motion): compare the keeps-its-links pins live, not by a path hash\n\nThe Adaptive spiral pin of #3837 compared an FNV hash of 5687 moves,\nrounded to 1e-4 mm, with a value recorded on Windows. On macOS aarch64\nthe last float bits differ and the hash changes. The Adaptive and Zigzag\npins now compute the same plan with around_part off (which never links\nby the ring law) in the same run, and assert the same moves and notes\nexactly. Without the ring predicate both pins are red.\n\nFixes #3853\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
